Z||000000||Bugsy||02-10-2001||10:15 AM||||In the last 9 years Working for the same company, located in a suburb about 9 miles from the city, I've been snowed in at work.  This company figures that if you're at work, you might as well stay.  When my shift is over, the oncoming shift doesn't show up, and  we can't even get our cars out of the parkinglot.  Well, this time I not only got the last word.  My shift Supervisor got mad when 1/2 of our crew left against his orders.   He yelled at me for defending them, told me that if we can't handle the weather to move to Texas, I informed him that we can't all afford a new Dodge Ram club cab 4x4, I then informed him that the price he was going to pay for my loyalty to the company (NOT!!) was a ride home AND a ride to work the next day...LOL.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Snowbound.jpg"> <BR>My poor Go-Cart is just a bit buried.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Buried.jpg"> <BR>The only good part about it is that the boss is totally ignoring me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||8
