Z||000004||Eric_PA||02-10-2001||11:30 AM||||The same thing happened to me at work this week. They expect onec you are at work to stay at work. They never called off the second shift and would issue acurances for those who left early. I stayed and ended up hitching a ride home since my car couldn't get out of the non plowed parking lot. As for the people who did show up for the second shift, they where sent back home. The company never notified them of a plant closing since the upper management never came in and as a result of that there were no calls made. Two days later I finally got my Jeep. Traded in the Sunfire and now having a great time this week. <P>I can't wait for the show here in PA. The Fiero isn't ready yet, do to all this snow, but yes today I'm driving arround with the roof up. 60 degrees here and snowing like heck a few days ago. Deffinately some weird weather.<P>||||reg||1
